    title: "Polo y servicio: forced labour for the Spanish crown",
    text: "Every Filipino man between sixteen and sixty under Spanish rule owed polo y servicio, forced labour, originally forty days a year, cutting timber in the mountains, building galleons at Cavite, and rowing or building churches, roads and bridges. Principales, the village elite, organised the levies and could buy exemption, as could anyone with the cash, the falla. Men were sometimes taken far from home in the planting season, and the shipbuilding drafts for the Manila galleons caused revolts, like that of Sumoroy in Samar in 1649. The labour was cut to fifteen days in 1884.",
    wiki: ["Polo y servicio", "Manila galleon"],
