    title: "Marshallese stick charts and atoll life",
    text: "The Marshall Islands are atolls, low rings of coral with poor sandy soil. People grew pandanus, breadfruit and coconut and fished lagoon and ocean. To sail between atolls, navigators studied how swells bent and crossed around islands, and taught this with stick charts, mattang and rebbelib, frameworks of coconut midribs tied with shells for islands. The charts were learning tools, not carried at sea; a navigator felt the swells through the canoe's hull, sometimes lying down to do so. Salt and fresh water came from a lens of rain floating under each islet, drawn from shallow wells.",
